  message: "Done in PR #1950 (e8fe59d786). Root cause: _detect_source_roots collected only directories named src, so a flat-layout member's files were named by repo path (packages.pkg-c.pkg_c.tools) and nothing in the tree was pkg_c. A directory below the repo root with a pyproject.toml / setup.py / setup.cfg, no src root of its own, and a child setuptools' flat-layout discovery would install is now a source root; it covers only those packages (the member's tests/ keep repo names) and a package name two flat members supply roots neither. The filed pkg_c.tools.Loud().go() shape failed in ANY layout (_resolve_call_target lacked WI-lovun's dotted-module spelling, so the constructor resolver typed the result as external); fixed in the same PR. CLOSURE EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run on merged dev through production `hypergumbo survey` (fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/fixtures/py): 0 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes (was 4); import pkg_c -> packages/pkg-c/pkg_c/__init__.py file node; pkg_c.tools.shout() -> tools.py shout function; pkg_c.tools.Loud().go() -> instantiates Loud class + calls Loud.go (method-call-recovery-linker, as tools.Loud().go() already did); from pkg_c import tools in the member's __init__ -> tools.py file node. Control ctl_flat (same package at the repo root): no pkg_c external_symbol, unchanged. Corpus A/B: firecracker 67 edges moved, all read correct; poetry/pants/fastapi/django/pretix 0."  # 2f23
